# L §4.6 Past the last row: "last(x[k], d) reads the latest row whose span began on or before d; its value is marked
# held in meta and in the register, so the carry is written where it is read (D-3)."  L §8.2 held entry.
# Rows: 1 for 2026-01..2026-03, 2 for 2026-05..2026-06; last(n, 2026-09-15) is the row from 2026-05: 2.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input n: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  n = 1 governs 2026-01..2026-03
  n = 2 governs 2026-05..2026-06

ask q1: last(n, 2026-09-15)
=== expect
q1: 2
  held: n = 2 (v), read for 2026-09-15
  cut 2026-12-31
